# Cloudflare Pages response headers (added 2026-11-20).
# ONE rule on purpose: Pages applies every rule that matches a path and joins a
# header set twice with a comma, so overlapping rules would produce
# "Cache-Control: a, b". Keep it to a single /* block.
#
# max-age=300: a browser re-checks at most every 5 minutes, and Pages answers a
# re-check with a 304 (ETag) when nothing changed. Each deploy replaces the files
# on Cloudflare's edge atomically, so there is no purge step and no ?v= / ?t=
# cache-buster needed anywhere.
#
# CORS: catalog-page.js fetch()es datasets-index.json from appen.com, a different
# origin. <script> and <link> tags don't need it; the fetch does.
/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
